From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 21:43:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] strip: delete Zed-cloud edit-prediction machinery from the
 engine

Sever every Zed-account / Zed-hosted coupling from edit prediction so it
only ever targets a user-provided self-hosted model. Removes from
EditPredictionStore the client/user_store/llm_token fields and the cloud
request paths they fed: the /predict_edits/v3 + /predict_edits/raw
(Baseten) completion paths, /predict_edits/accept|reject|settled, the
/edit_prediction_experiments A/B machinery, usage/quota tracking, and the
training-data-collection pipeline (capture_example.rs, license_detection.rs,
example_spec.rs, settled/feedback workers, open-source detection). The
self-hosted Zeta-format path (Ollama / OpenAI-compatible) and the BYO-key
Mercury/Codestral providers are kept.

zeta.rs now keeps only the custom-server branch; the delegate drops the
account-billing gate and reports no data-collection/usage; the registry and
status-bar button drop all sign-in/usage/billing/experiments/upsell UI and
the user_store threading. The rate-predictions and capture-example training
UI (rate_prediction_modal.rs) is removed.

The edit_prediction test suite is dropped: it was built entirely on a
FakeServer harness mimicking the removed Zed-cloud /predict_edits endpoints,
so it cannot run against the self-hosted-only path. A self-hosted test
harness is a follow-up.

cloud_api_client / cloud_api_types deps removed from edit_prediction;
cloud_llm_client is kept for shared types only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
